            <ArticleTitle>Primary Burkitt's lymphoma of the appendix.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Appendicitis is a very rare presenting symptom of abdominal Burkitt's lymphoma. Only four cases have previously been identified in the literature, all of them males. This is the first reported case of a female as well as the youngest and is representative of the therapeutic considerations in this unusual manifestation of the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
